      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary angioscopy, intravascular ultrasound, and angiography were compared in 20 patients regarding their sensitivity and specificity in the detection of thrombus. Although all imaging procedures demonstrate a high specificity, only coronary angioscopy has a sensitivity high enough to provide sufficient evidence of thrombus, even in patients with stable angina."},
